  "title": "Lei Aurea abolishes slavery in Brazil",
  "summary": "On 13 May 1888 Princess Isabel, acting as regent while Emperor Pedro II was abroad, signed Law No. 3,353, the Lei Aurea. Its two articles declared slavery extinct in Brazil. Parliament had passed the bill in about five days, over opposition from slaveholding senators led by the Baron of Cotegipe.",
